             `what the Act points at` IS EMPTY
             `the Act's words` IS "\"Accountant-General\" means the Accountant-General of Singapore;"

-- Entry 3 of s 2(1): act
-- src:176 | “act”, in relation to an offence or civil wrong, includes a series of
-- src:177 | acts, and words which refer to acts done are to be construed as
-- src:178 | extending to illegal omissions;
@ref s 2(1) "act" (src:176-178)
`s 2(1) definition 03: act` MEANS
    Definition
        WITH terms IS LIST "act"
             kind IS Includes
             `what the Act names` IS LIST "a series of acts", "illegal omissions"
             `what the Act points at` IS EMPTY
             `the Act's words` IS "\"act\", in relation to an offence or civil wrong, includes a series of acts, and words which refer to acts done are to be construed as extending to illegal omissions;"

-- Entry 4 of s 2(1): Act, Act of Parliament
-- src:180 | “Act” or “Act of Parliament” means an Act of the Parliament of
-- src:181 | Singapore and includes any Ordinance or Act of Singapore or
-- src:182 | Malaysia having the force of law in Singapore; and “Act”,
-- src:183 | when used in any subsidiary legislation, means the Act under
-- src:184 | the authority of which the subsidiary legislation was made;
@ref s 2(1) "Act"; "Act of Parliament" (src:180-184)
`s 2(1) definition 04: Act` MEANS
    Definition
        WITH terms IS LIST "Act", "Act of Parliament"
             kind IS `Means and includes`
             `what the Act names` IS LIST "an Act of the Parliament of Singapore", "Ordinance or Act of Singapore or Malaysia having the force of law in Singapore", "the Act under the authority of which the subsidiary legislation was made"
             `what the Act points at` IS EMPTY
             `the Act's words` IS "\"Act\" or \"Act of Parliament\" means an Act of the Parliament of Singapore and includes any Ordinance or Act of Singapore or Malaysia having the force of law in Singapore; and \"Act\", when used in any subsidiary legislation, means the Act under the authority of which the subsidiary legislation was made;"

